{
  "analysis": "Critical findings: SQLite 3.45.1, NO indexes at all, ~212K senses rows, ~152K words. The original query's correlated subqueries each do a full table scan of senses (212K rows) for EVERY row passing the HAVING filter. The key optimization is to (1) limit the expensive per-row subqueries to only the top 500 results, and (2) replace correlated subqueries with a single-pass window function approach.",
  "plan": "1. Count rows passing HAVING filter to understand scale. 2. Run original query with timing to get baseline. 3. Write and test optimized query using CTEs + window function instead of correlated subqueries. 4. Verify outputs match.",
  "commands": [
    {
    "keystrokes": "sqlite3 /app/oewn.sqlite \"SELECT COUNT(*) FROM (SELECT w.wordid, w.word, COUNT(DISTINCT s.synsetid) AS total_synsets, COUNT(*) AS total_senses, COUNT(DISTINCT syn.domainid) AS distinct_domains, COUNT(DISTINCT syn.posid) AS distinct_posids FROM words w JOIN senses s ON w.wordid = s.wordid JOIN synsets syn ON s.synsetid = syn.synsetid GROUP BY w.wordid, w.word HAVING total_synsets >= 2 AND distinct_domains >= 2 AND total_senses >= 2);\"\n",
    "duration": 10.0
    }
